  "page": 364,
  "line": 1,
  "situation": "The scripture band is nearly empty here because the plate cites almost nothing, and that is correct — §32 pleads the mysteries themselves, not texts about them, so what the leaf needs is its Greek opened. The two columns are not an antithesis — the Person on the left, the life on the right. *Ἀπαρχὰς αἵματος*, the firstfruits of thy blood, is the Circumcision counted as the first shedding, eight days old; *ἀπαρχή* is the firstfruits word of 1 Cor. xv. 20. The article is given a reason for standing in a plea about the Passion.",
